\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Jesus is my Saviour,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I am on my journey;
\par Jesus, you have ever travelled.
\par Out of your immense love,
\par You walked long distances.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And you suffered in life's journey.
\par You suffered for my sake;
\par You are the Almighty,
\par For me, I worth nothing.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  You show love to sinners,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Make them righteous people;
\par And show your compassion for them.
\par You came down from heaven,
\par And went round your kinsmen;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par You kept moving round your people.
\par 'Twas your wish to redeem,
\par Mankind from all evil,
\par And from all punishments.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  When you made your Journeys,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Throughout all Judea,
\par It turned out to be all blessings.
\par You did good to people;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Preached the Word to them all;
\par Healed the sick, and delivered them,
\par \cf1 Defiled hunger and thirst;\cf0 
\par Long walks and wake-keeping, \tab 
\par You did your Father's will.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. Throughout all my journey,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Prompt me of Thy journey,
\par Let me watch and follow Thy path.
\par Let me love my kinsmen,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Just as you love me too.
\par Let me also seek their welfare,
\par All day long and at might,
\par Care for me on my way,
\par Also in my guest room.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The love of my Lord God,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 The grace of my Saviour,
\par And the peace of the Holy Ghost.
\par It gives me much pleasure,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And my consolation,
\par On which I do depend so much.
\par My good Lord, cares for me,
\par Let me look up to you,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj Till I return safely.       \f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

